        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 432,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 98,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "This equation will also be referred to as the (local) continuity equation. Because there is no separate evolution equation for the pressure the local continuity equation acts as a constraint on the flow field."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 8971,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 434,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 100,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Because free surface flows are considered a separate equation to determine the free surface location  is required. To obtain an expression for the free surface the continuity equation is integrated over the depth:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 9051,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 436,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 102,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Now it is assumed that the water surface is always composed of the same particles. This is justified due to exclusion of wave overturning. The vertical velocity of a particle located at the free surface is therefore equal to the material derivative of the free surface and this results in the kinematic boundary condition at free surface:"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 9060,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 437,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 103,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "(1.7)"
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
